@startuml direct-rialto-state-machine
title direct-rialto PlayerStateMachine (AampPlayerStateMachine.cpp)

[*] --> IDLE

state "Session active\n(every state except IDLE, FLUSHING, ERROR)" as ACTIVE {
	state PIPELINE_CREATED
	state SOURCES_ATTACHING
	state SOURCES_ATTACHED
	state PLAYING
	state PAUSED
	state FLUSHED
}

IDLE --> PIPELINE_CREATED : onPipelineLoaded\n[Configure: load() succeeded]
PIPELINE_CREATED --> SOURCES_ATTACHING : onSourceAttaching\n[first source attach starts]
SOURCES_ATTACHING --> SOURCES_ATTACHED : onAllSourcesAttached\n[allSourcesAttached() accepted]

SOURCES_ATTACHED --> PLAYING : onPlaybackStarted\n[Rialto PLAYING]
SOURCES_ATTACHED --> PAUSED : onPlaybackPaused\n[Rialto PAUSED: pre-roll pause()]
PLAYING --> PAUSED : onPlaybackPaused\n[Rialto PAUSED]
PAUSED --> PLAYING : onPlaybackStarted\n[Rialto PLAYING]

SOURCES_ATTACHED --> FLUSHING : onFlush
PLAYING --> FLUSHING : onFlush
PAUSED --> FLUSHING : onFlush
FLUSHED --> FLUSHING : onFlush\n[rapid second seek]

FLUSHING --> FLUSHED : onFlushComplete\n[SEEK_DONE, setPosition failed,\nno pipeline, or wait timeout]
FLUSHED --> PLAYING : onPlaybackStarted\n[Rialto PLAYING]
FLUSHED --> PAUSED : onPlaybackPaused\n[Rialto PAUSED]

ACTIVE --> IDLE : onStop [state != IDLE]\nonReconfigure
ACTIVE --> ERROR : onError\n[Rialto FAILURE]
FLUSHING --> ERROR : onError\n[Rialto FAILURE]
ERROR --> IDLE : onStop / onReconfigure

note right of FLUSHING
  onStop and onReconfigure have no transition here:
  Stop() and Configure() first wait for the flush to
  end (waitForFlushComplete), so they never see
  FLUSHING.  Any event with no transition is
  ignored with a WARN, e.g. onPlaybackPaused
  in PAUSED, onPlaybackStarted in FLUSHING.
end note

note left of IDLE
  IDLE: onStop is ignored quietly.
  onReconfigure stays IDLE.  onError is ignored
  (no session).  onSourceAttaching is accepted
  by the guard in IDLE and ERROR but has no
  transition there, so it logs a WARN.
end note

note bottom of ERROR
  Terminal until Stop(), a teardown Flush(), or a
  Configure() that rebuilds the pipeline moves the
  machine back to IDLE.  Only the first FAILURE
  (previous state not IDLE/ERROR) is reported to AAMP.
end note

note as THREADING
  Each event dispatch takes the state machine's mutex,
  so a single call is atomic.  A sequence such as
  "read currentState(), then act" is not.  The one
  sequence that must be atomic, entering FLUSHING after
  waiting for a previous flush, is serialised by the
  player's m_flushCallMutex.  Every transition wakes
  waitForFlushComplete().
end note
@enduml
